4. A sanity check against something you already know.$us$, $us$Commercial minutes → number of 30-second slots → price per slot.$us$, $us$The game broadcast runs ~3.5 hours, and roughly 23% of it is commercials, ~48 minutes, or ~96 thirty-second slots. Some go to network promos, so ~86 are sold at around $7M each: 86 × $7M ≈ $600M. Sanity check: that is ~$170M an hour of airtime, far above any other TV event, which fits the Super Bowl's ~115M-plus audience.$us$, true, null, 'size', $us${"firm":"BCG","round":"first round","est_minutes":10,"points_reward":70,"source":"us-bank"}$us$::jsonb, 'US'),
  ($us$US-G-07$us$, $us$How many public EV charging ports are there in California?$us$, 'guesstimate', $us$medium$us$, $us$# How many public EV charging ports are there in California?

