4. A sanity check against something you already know.$us$, $us$Segment households into Prime and non-Prime and estimate packages per household per week.$us$, $us$131M US households: ~55% (72M) have Prime and receive ~1.4 Amazon packages a week (~101M a week); the other ~59M receive ~0.25 a week (~15M). That is ~116M packages a week, ~16.5M a day, about 6B a year. Sanity check: 6B packages over 335M people is ~18 per person a year, about one every three weeks per person, which feels right.$us$, true, null, 'size', $us${"firm":"Bain","round":"first round","est_minutes":12,"points_reward":85,"source":"us-bank"}$us$::jsonb, 'US'),
